# conf.d is the RUNTIME override directory, bind-mounted over
# /etc/postgresql/conf.d by docker-compose.test.yml at container start. It is
# not a build input -- the Dockerfile never COPYs it -- so excluding it keeps
# an override edit from busting the build cache and keeps it out of the build
# context entirely.
#
# (An earlier version of this comment also claimed excluding it prevents an
# override being "baked into the image where it would shadow the ARG defaults".
# That was wrong: nothing COPYs conf.d, so it could never have been baked in
# regardless of this file. The real effects are cache invalidation and context
# size.)
conf.d/
